=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: r7
diagnosis_text:
The ospfd process on r7 crashed and exited approximately 2 minutes after lab startup. The FRR log on r7 shows the sequence clearly: ospfd started and read its configuration at 13:56:42, successfully completed a Database Description exchange with r6 (router-ID 16.1.4.1) at 13:57:29, then abruptly shut down at 13:58:14 with the message "Client 'ospf' (session id 0) encountered an error and is shutting down." Zebra immediately de-installed the 64 OSPF routes ospfd had installed, including r7's loopbacks (17.1.x.0/24), its LAN (70.0.0.0/8), and the R6–R7 link (67.0.0.0/8). Since ospfd is no longer running, r7 originates no LSAs, r6's eth2 (67.1.1.1/8) has zero OSPF neighbors, and the rest of the domain — including r1 — never receives r7's prefixes. The on-disk `/etc/frr/frr.conf` is completely intact with the correct `router ospf` block and all six `network` statements, and `/etc/frr/daemons` correctly sets `ospfd=yes`, so no configuration file needs to be changed. The root cause is that ospfd on r7 terminated abnormally after forming its adjacency, leaving the daemon absent while the config is healthy. The corrective fix is to restart FRR on r7 (`service frr restart` or `systemctl restart frr`), which will re-launch ospfd, load the existing frr.conf, re-establish the Full adjacency with r6, and re-flood r7's LSAs so that r1 and all other OSPF speakers re-learn the 17.x.x.x, 67.0.0.0/8, and 70.0.0.0/8 prefixes.
=== END ===